# .janitor-secret-allow — exemptions for the secret scans (TRDD-FNPDFZWU increment 2c).
# Read by scripts/lib/staged_secret_scan.py from the INDEX (commit scan) or from the TIP COMMIT of the scanned range (push and publish
# scans). A list that is not committed exempts nothing. A commit message, release notes and CHANGELOG text can never be exempted.
#
# One entry per line, four TAB-separated fields:
#   <kind>  <path>  line:<sha256 hex of the line text, no newline> | blob:<full git blob oid>  <reason, non-empty>
# A finding with no line number can only be exempted by a blob: entry. Any malformed line makes the scan exit 2.
#
# RULE: a line: entry is only for a value judged FAKE. A real secret is never exempted: rotate it, then rewrite the history.
# WHY an unsalted line hash is acceptable: an entry exists only for a line that is itself in a pushed blob, so the hash gives an
# attacker nothing the blob does not already hold. When such a line is later removed from history, its entry must go too.
#
# Ready-made lines for the blocking findings: staged_secret_scan.py --print-allow-entries [--range <rev-list args>]
# (it prints REVIEW-ME as the reason; replace it with who judged the value fake, and when).
